  "label": "two_men mapped as 'the second one'",
  "description": "The bottom text 'the first one can't sing when you put chains on it' implies a contrast with 'the second one', which is visually represented by the two Black men in the historical photograph. The mapping identifies the two men as 'the second one', contrasting them with the bicycle ('the first one'). This mapping is established through the textual reference to 'the first one' and the visual context of the two men being the only other entities in the image, creating a binary comparison.",
